<title>UK: Siebe wins new orders worth 85 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Siebe wins new orders worth 85 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Siebe Plc said on Wednesday its control systems division won new orders worth over 85 million stg based on its Foxboro Intelligent Automation software system.</p>
<p>The company said one of the contracts was from Hong Kong's Mass Transit Rail Corporation, owned by the Hong Kong government.  </p>
<p>Siebe said it also won a &quot;substantial order&quot; from Formosa Petrochemical Corporation, a subsidiary of Taiwan's Formosa Plastics Corporation.</p>
<p>Siebe will supply a variety of systems for a 21 million tonne annual capacity refinery in Mai-Liao in Taiwan.</p>
<p>In the gas sector, Siebe won orders in Malaysia, Oman, Qatar, and Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
